<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh June copper output falls 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh June copper output falls 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakh copper output fell by 2.9 percent in June from May's level and zinc output rose by 3.4 percent, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures for Kazakhstan's production of metals (all figures in tonnes)-</p>
<p>					June 97    May 97    Jan-June 97</p>
<p> COPPER				25,947     26,718    140,355</p>
<p>  mth/mtn pct change	     -2.9	 +2.7	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change		+14.0	 -4.1	 -7.0</p>
<p> ZINC				  16,419     15,874     90,431</p>
<p>  mtn/mth pct change	     +3.4	 +7.3	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change		+15.4	 +1.5	+10.6</p>
<p> LEAD				   5,824	7,924     36,728</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	    -26.5	 -2.7	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr pct change		-10.5	+39.0	+14.5</p>
<p> BAUXITE			    331,900    292,200  1,577,300</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	    +13.6	+20.5	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +4.7	 -0.9	 +0.5</p>
<p> ALUMINA			     89,177     92,060    543,598</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     -3.1	 +3.1	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +2.8	 +2.8	 +3.4</p>
<p> TITANIUM			     1.505	1.530	9.075</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     -1.6	 +2.0	  n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    +33.0	+53.9	+58.1</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
